ant takes in through its roots from what it makes. The contrast section puts the producer idea against the soil-as-food and water-as-food readings on the same plant so the boundary is visible, and the close checks whether the learner now recognizes the plant, not the soil or the water, as the maker of the food.\"\\n    },\\n    \"neighbours\": [\\n      {\\n        \"kind\": \"heading\",\\n        \"reason\": \"Signals the opening concrete case so the learner knows this section sets up the windowsill plant and the question to consider.\",\\n        \"role\": \"orienting-heading\",\\n        \"teaching_block_id\": \"orient-b1\"\\n      },\\n      {\\n        \"kind\": \"paragraph\",\\n        \"reason\": \"Presents the potted classroom plant on the windowsill beside the cup of water as the single anchor held across the lesson, without naming food sources.\",\\n        \"role\": \"case-setup\",\\n        \"teaching_block_id\": \"orient-b1\"\\n      },\\n      {\\n        \"kind\": \"heading\",\\n        \"reason\": \"Introduces the category term \\'producer\\' to be fixed, keeping attention on the definition rather than the mechanism.\",\\n        \"role\": \"term-heading\",\\n        \"teaching_block_id\": \"explain-b1\"\\n      },\\n      {\\n        \"kind\": \"paragraph\",\\n        \"reason\": \"States the single idea that a producer is a living thing that makes its own food and that the windowsill plant is a producer, with no sunlight or mechanism yet.\",\\n        \"role\": \"definition\",\\n        \"teaching_block_id\": \"explain-b1\"\\n      }\\n    ],\\n    \"reason\": \"Cues the learner to pause and commit to a personal guess about where the plant\\'s food comes from before any explanation, so the explanation has a held model to revise; the interaction itself is authored separately.\",\\n    \"role\": \"commit-prompt\",\\n    \"teaching_block\": {\\n      \"brief\": \"Present the concrete case: a potted classroom plant on the windowsill, sitting next to a 